{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You shall not commit adultery.</b> נִאוּף is only with a married woman, as it says ״מוֹת יוּמַת הַנּוֹאֵף וְהַנּוֹאָפֶת״ (Leviticus 20), and it says ״הָאִשָּׁה הַמְנָאֶפֶת תַּחַת אִישָׁהּ תִּקַּח אֶת זָרִים״ (Ezekiel 16)." "<b>You shall not steal.</b> Scripture speaks of kidnapping; ״לֹא תִּגְנֹבוּ״ (Leviticus 19) speaks of stealing money. Or perhaps this too is about stealing money and the other about kidnapping? You would say: a matter learned from its context — just as לֹא תִרְצָח, לֹא תִנְאָף speak of something liable to the death penalty by the court, so too לֹא תִגְנֹב speaks of something liable to the death penalty by the court (Sanhedrin 86a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:22.768466950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}